// Universal narrative quest system for AI Dungeon.
//
// CORE DESIGN:
// - Quests are written by the model in a DEDICATED QUEST TURN:
//   a short, clean request (Story Cards + recent story + one example)
//   that ends in "TITLE:" so the model only has to finish four lines.
//   (Hidden JSON / tags inside a normal story turn were ignored by the
//   model in testing, so this version does not rely on them.)
// - The model decides HOW GOOD the moment is (SCORE, 0-100).
//   The script decides what to do with it (MIN_QUEST_SCORE).
// - Also indexes Story Cards that are NOT currently triggered.
// - Optional integrations are strictly opt-in.
// - Quest state is stored in state.questDirector.
// - The visible quest layer is a managed Story Card and can be disabled.
// - YOU mark a quest as finished by editing that Story Card:
//     [x] = completed      [-] = abandoned
// - Quests are narrative invitations, not predefined rewards/payoffs.
//
// IMPORTANT:
// The three hook tabs (Input / Context / Output) must contain only
// ONE "modifier(text)" wrapper each.
// When combining this with other scripts, keep one modifier and call
// QuestDirector.input/context/output from that existing wrapper.
// Hook order: see the comments inside the three hook files.

/* ============================================================
   CREATOR CONFIGURATION
   ============================================================ */

const QUEST_DIRECTOR_ENABLED = true;

/*
Chance of starting a QUEST TURN on an eligible turn.

IMPORTANT:
A quest turn REPLACES that turn's normal narration with a short
"New quest" notice (the model is busy designing the quest).
Press Retry afterwards to get the story response to your action.
So keep this low.

0.08 = rare
0.12 = occasional / balanced
0.20 = frequent

For your FIRST test set it to 1, then put it back.
*/
const QUEST_ACTIVATION_CHANCE = 0.12;

/*
Minimum number of turns that must pass after a QUEST IS CREATED
before the script can attempt to create another one.
*/
const MIN_TURNS_BETWEEN_QUESTS = 6;

/*
Minimum number of turns between attempts to generate a new quest.
Failed attempts do not create quests, but still observe this cooldown.
*/
const MIN_TURNS_BETWEEN_ATTEMPTS = 3;

/*
Maximum number of active quests at once.
*/
const MAX_ACTIVE_QUESTS = 3;

/*
How many finished quests are remembered for duplicate prevention.
*/
const MAX_COMPLETED_QUESTS = 24;

/*
How long a quest can remain active.

0 = quests never expire.
*/
const QUEST_EXPIRATION_TURNS = 80;

/*
Allow the model to create main-story quests.
*/
const ALLOW_MAIN_STORY_QUESTS = true;

/*
Allow the model to create side quests.
*/
const ALLOW_SIDE_QUESTS = true;

/*
Allow quests to naturally lead into follow-up quests.
A follow-up can only continue a quest YOU already finished.
*/
const ALLOW_QUEST_CHAINS = true;

/*
Maximum chain depth.
0 = original quest
1 = first follow-up
2 = second follow-up
3 = third follow-up
*/
const MAX_CHAIN_DEPTH = 3;

/*
THE "RIGHT MOMENT" FILTER.

The model rates how strong the narrative opportunity is (0-100).
A quest is only accepted when the score reaches this number.
Lower = more quests. Higher = only very strong opportunities.
If the model forgets to give a score, the quest is accepted.
*/
const MIN_QUEST_SCORE = 72;

/*
Higher threshold required for a quest chain.
*/
const MIN_CHAIN_SCORE = 82;

/*
Language of the QUEST TEXT written by the model.

"auto" = match the dominant English/Spanish language of the story.
You can force "en" or "es".
*/
const QUEST_LANGUAGE = "auto";

/*
Language of the Story Card / notices (the interface).
This is independent from the quest text language above.

"en"   = always English
"es"   = always Spanish
"auto" = follows the story language (never flips on one short phrase)
*/
const QUEST_DISPLAY_LANGUAGE = "en";

/*
Show the managed Quest Director Story Card.

false = the quest system still works,
but no quest display card is maintained
(then you cannot mark quests as finished by hand).
*/
const SHOW_QUEST_DISPLAY = true;

/*
Add ONE short line to normal turns reminding the model of the
active quests, so the narration stays aware of them.
*/
const REMIND_MODEL_OF_ACTIVE_QUESTS = true;

/*
Useful while testing.

true = the Story Card shows a "Last checks" section that explains,
turn by turn, why a quest was or was not created.
Set to false once everything works.
*/
const QUEST_DIRECTOR_DEBUG = true;

/*
Context limits.

The quest request is built from these pieces. Everything is also
limited by info.maxChars (the real context limit of the game),
so the request can never be cut off by the server.
*/
const WORLD_INDEX_MAX_CHARS = 4500;
const INTEGRATION_MAX_CHARS = 1500;
const STORY_EXCERPT_CHARS = 2500;

/*
Keep the visible quest card comfortably small.
*/
const DISPLAY_MAX_CHARS = 1500;


